- A CoreDNS ConfigMap with no `Corefile` key: the writer dies (k328, a [WARN] on STDERR), the probe moves on or reports nothing. They still disagree there.
- The writer repairs the duplicate-hosts Corefile that crashes CoreDNS; the probe does not detect it.
- Server-block keys with a port are matched by zone only (as before k338) -- fine for :53, say so if another port appears.

Done = writer and probe agree on each case (t/338 extended), or an ADR line saying which case is deliberately not handled.

